  "approach": "Teach the default order (noun, then descriptive adjective), muy as an unchanging intensifier, and the small set of words that go before the noun, including buen and gran.",
  "coverage": [
    "Descriptive adjectives usually follow the noun: una mujer alta, un coche pequeño",
    "Muy goes right before the adjective and never changes: una mujer muy alta, unas casas muy grandes",
    "Never mucho before an adjective: muy grande, not mucho grande",
    "Numbers and quantity words go before: dos libros, muchos amigos, otro día",
    "Bueno and malo can go before and shorten: un buen amigo, un mal día",
    "Gran before a noun means great; grande after means big: un gran hombre, un hombre grande",
    "Colors and nationalities always go after: un carro rojo, una película mexicana"
  ],
